  m_text: "At dusk where day and night entwine, choose first the shade that drinks
    both fire and frost.\n\nNext, take what crowns the timid king\u2014bright metal
    without weight.\n\nThird, swear the oath of mariners and sages who stare into
    depth without blinking.\n\nFourth, follow where the forest keeps its counsel.\n\nLast,
    return to the color of drums and warnings, where every tale begins and ends in
    breath."
